; SIXTEEN BYTES MOVED UP 885 CELLS  leaving the source EMPTY; Entered where
; the source begins and it leaves the pointer on the source's last cell;
;
; THE THIRD OF THE 885 FAMILY  and the distance is not a coincidence: every
; mode here puts its sixteen byte working value exactly 885 cells above the
; cipher's state  so the three routines that cross that gap are one text
; each; block/copy16 goes DOWN and stages  block/move16 goes DOWN and does
; not  and this one comes back UP;
;
; UP IS A SEPARATE ROUTINE AND NOT A PARAMETER  because an include carries an
; offset and not a direction: the offset shifts where a block's frame starts
; and cannot turn R885 into L885; That is the same limit block/copy16's
; header records about distances  seen from the other side;
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
  [-R885+L885]
